    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-83641: E[N]=(0·10+1·7+2·2+3·1)/20=0.7. q-79697: multiplying by x² and collecting y gives y'-xy=x², with x≠0. q-16400: moving the y term left and dividing by 2 gives y'+2sin(x)y=(1+3cos(x))/2. q-103567: option 3 becomes y'-xe^(2x)y=cos(x) after multiplication by y, on its original domain y≠0; the other choices are nonlinear. q-103551: option 0 already has the linear form y'+P(x)y=Q(x), with x>0. q-106744: Av=(1,-2), whose component ratios to v are 1 and 2, so v is not an eigenvector. q-106775: Av=(16,-8), whose ratios to v are 8 and 2, so v is not an eigenvector. q-75732: Cv=-2(0,-2)=(0,4), matching option 3. q-75735: Au=(1/2)(2,0)=(1,0), matching option 4. q-107837: both component equations give c=2. q-75611: the first component gives 7=2k+1, hence k=3, and the second component also holds. q-75730: inverse matrices reciprocate nonzero eigenvalues, and nonzero scalar multiples preserve eigenvectors and eigenvalues, so all three statements are true. q-77547: conjugating x₂ and multiplying by i gives (-6,2+i); adding x₁ gives (-3-8i,-2+3i). q-76039: conjugation reverses the imaginary signs and leaves -3 unchanged. q-130890: ac+bd=1(-3)+(-1)(-5)=2. q-76050: ad+bc=(-6)(-6)+1·7=43. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation is based on the captured worked solutions.",
